  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the hateful dating request scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the hateful dating request scene, which is explicitly framed as a request made by the speaker (the person making the request) who is visually represented by Adolf Hitler. The text 'i just want a girl who laugh at my racist jokes and cuddle me is it to much to ask!' uses the first-person pronoun 'me', directly projecting the user's identity onto the speaker of the request. This creates a semiotic projection where the user identifies with the speaker's persona and the hateful message. The projection is onto the entire scene, which includes both the visual material of Adolf Hitler and the textual material of the request, as the user is identifying with the speaker's romantic ideal and the hateful context in which it is presented.",
